es": ["Open seat: Dan McKee (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island's governorship is open this year after Dan McKee lost the Democratic primary to Helena Foulkes. Foulkes now faces Republican Aaron Guckian and independents including Ken Block, who has spent heavily on ads and unveiled a detailed agenda. Polling throughout the fall has shown Foulkes leading by double digits, with the most recent surveys giving her margins of roughly 11 to 34 points. Guckian's campaign finance reports show cash-flow problems, limiting his ability to compete on the airwaves.\n\nThe state's Democratic lean, the unanimous Solid or Safe Democratic ratings from every major forecaster, and prediction markets pricing Foulkes near 96-99% all point the same direction. The main uncertainty is the final margin, since Block and other independents could draw enough votes to keep Foulkes below 50%, but the outcome itself is not seriously in doubt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9941, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9927, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9969, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9973, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-1